  "answer": "Project Zenith is a cloud storage optimization initiative launched in Q3 2023, led by Marcus Cole, aimed at enhancing security and accessibility. The project has progressed through design and development phases, with Omar Jensen leading development. Key milestones include the successful testing of a secure file sharing prototype ahead of schedule, with UI enhancements planned for October. The project has secured a strategic partnership with TechInnovate to leverage their AI technology, which is now in the implementation phase. The team has expanded to include Mike Chen (machine learning) and Lisa Ray (cloud computing). The budget has been adjusted to $550,000 to cover unforeseen expenses and real-time analytics integration, with an additional $55,000 allocated for compliance training and audits. Security protocols have been updated to include multi-factor authentication and encryption at rest, effective January next year."
